{
  "pedal": "Boss CS-3 Compression Sustainer — focused reamp: guitar excerpts over a quiet probe tone (mono)",
  "comment": "Short excerpts of the guitar DI dataset (captures/di/) over a steady 9 kHz sine 50 dB under the guitar's peak (the probe: under the pedal's threshold at every Sustain position, so it shows the gain at every moment without being compressed itself; where the guitar is loud the gain is read from the guitar). Level and Tone stay at 12:00 throughout: only Sustain and Attack turn, one per step. What each kind of take is for: stabs (a chord, then silence) = the recovery after each hit, read on the probe; funk = fast picking at the dataset's hottest level (attacks, what the release leaves between strokes); chords = sustained notes held at the ceiling as they die away; dynamics = soft to hard picks (the static curve on real notes); lead = held out of any fit. At the main setting (everything at 12:00) also: the probe alone (the idle gain), the stabs without the probe (does the probe change what the pedal does?), funk twice (the pedal against itself: the method's floor), funk 12 dB down and chords 12 and 24 dB down (a ladder: the same playing crossing the threshold at different points). With Sustain fully clockwise the probe is 10 dB quieter still (-60 dB: the threshold is lower there). Sustain 7:00: the pedal's path with the compressor hardly working. Clock positions: 7:00 = fully counter-clockwise, 5:00 = fully clockwise. Takes ordered so each step turns one knob.",
  "quiet_dbfs": -60,
  "knobs": [
    "Level",
    "Tone",
    "Attack",
    "Sustain"
  ],
